 #### 3.2 Figures — 4–8 publication-grade
 
+**Mandatory:** Load `publication-figures` before planning or drawing figures;
+require every delegated figure agent to load it and follow these same rules.
+Use its FigTree schematic workflow; illustrated reference-led overviews are the default for method/proposal overviews.
+Before drawing these overviews, read the `publication-figures` companion `illustrated-overviews.md`;
+inspect actual reference PNGs (not article prose) to guide composition.
+Assess reference likeness separately from the content/layout pass.
+Display one style preview and obtain user approval before bulk redesign.
+Preserve data plots from decoration; use its chart rules for data-backed quantitative plots, not schematic layouts.
+Apply its render-inspect-repair loop and final-size gate to every figure.
+Explicit user or venue visual requirements override aesthetic defaults only, never grounding or readability gates.
+
 **Open:** `references/02-figures-publication-grade.md`.
 
